# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every artefact this repository produces ultimately executes inside a Linux
# container (the worker sandbox) or on a Linux runner. A Windows checkout with
# the default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrote LF to CRLF, which baked
# `#!/usr/bin/env node\r` into `infra/docker/worker-sandbox/provider-entrypoint.mjs`
# and made the built sandbox image fail at exit 127:
#
#   /usr/bin/env: 'node\r': No such file or directory
#
# Linux CI never saw this because Linux checkouts are already LF. Forcing LF on
# checkout for all text files keeps Windows-built images identical to CI-built
# ones. Node, TypeScript, Prettier and ESLint all handle LF on Windows.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Files copied into Linux images or run by a shebang MUST be LF regardless of
# any future relaxation of the rule above.
*.sh                                          text eol=lf
*.mjs                                         text eol=lf
Dockerfile                                    text eol=lf
infra/docker/worker-sandbox/provider-entrypoint.mjs text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts, should any be added, need CRLF.
*.bat                                         text eol=crlf
*.cmd                                         text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
